<title>FRANCE: Private firms key to defence shakeout - minister.</title>
<headline>Private firms key to defence shakeout - minister.</headline>
<dateline>LE BOURGET, France 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's defence minister said on Thursday that Europe's industrial consolidation depended on strong private sector companies, to respond to competition from the United States.</p>
<p>&quot;If we want to create strong companies in the face of American competition in Europe, they need to be private companies,&quot; Volker Ruhe told reporters at the Paris air show.</p>
<p>Ruhe was speaking on the eve of a keynote speech to be given by French Socialist Prime Minister Lionel Jospin here on Saturday. Industry executives are eager to hear the government's policy on Thomson-CSF and Aerospatiale.</p>
</text>
